Z||000009||Carrolles||01-25-2001||08:14 AM||||I'd use what is designed for it.  You don't want to have to go through replacement again if it doesn't work out.  The new seals cost only a couple of bucks and can be gotten from AutoZone, etc.<P>Take the old ones with you to match up to new ones.  They come in different thicknesses.<p>[This message has been edited by Carrolles (edited 01-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||theogre||01-25-2001||07:26 PM||||You must use the seals made for it. anything else will leak. maybe not right away but it will leak. Your dealing with 200-300PSI and allot of heat. ||||reg||1
